A planet is detected orbiting a star. The following measurements are available: Stellar mass: 1.0 M☉ Orbital period: 12 days Radial-velocity semi-amplitude of the star: 15 m/s Orbital eccentricity: 0.20 Orbital inclination: 60° Task: Determine the mass of the planet from the available information. 
Reason through what needs to be calculated and provide the result.

Your result should be of this form:

{
"result": {
"planet_mass": number,
"unit": "M_Earth"
}
}

In addition to the result, provide the sequence of steps, calculations, and physical relations you would use to obtain it.

A hypothetical particle decay is proposed:

X → e⁺ + γ

Task: Reason over the proposed process, determine the physical properties of the initial particle X that can be inferred from the final state, and identify whether the process is physically allowed. Consider all relevant conservation laws and quantum numbers. Determine whether X can be a Standard Model particle. Do not assume properties that cannot be inferred from the process. If multiple physically possible sets of properties exist, provide all possible sets. If the proposed process is not physically possible because it violates a required conservation law, provide a single result with "None" for the relevant properties.

Your result should be of this form:

{
  "possible_properties": [
    {
      "electric_charge_X": -2 | -1 | -2/3 | -1/3 | 0 | 1/3 | 2/3 | 1 | 2
      "lepton_number_X": integer 
      "baryon_number_X": integer
      "color_X": "singlet" | "triplet" | "antitriplet" | "sextet" | "antisextet" | "octet"
      "can_be_SM_particle": true | false 
    }
  ]
}

Each dictionary in "possible_properties" represents one physically possible set of properties for X. Include all physically possible sets and do not include physically impossible sets.

Find any arXiv paper(s) from the Pierre Auger Collaboration (must be one of the authors) whose arXiv IDs start with 2602. (i.e., papers submitted in February 2026).

Output the results only as a JSON object in the following format:

{"papers": [{"arxiv_id": "str", "title": "str"}, ...]}

If no matching papers are found, output only:

{"papers": []}

